{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1128376-dealing-with-mta-s-equivalent-of-netrunning","id":1128376,"title":"Dealing with MtA's equivalent of NetRunning","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-13T02:56:37-07:00","id":1128376,"title":"Dealing with MtA's equivalent of NetRunning","content":"In some roleplaying games, there can occur times in which a single player is hived off from the other players to such an extent that they effectively have a 1-on-1 session. In Cyberpunk 2020, it was NetRunning. In Shadowrun, it was decking. In Mage the Ascension...it can be Correspondence/Digital Web access...but can also occur if you have a Spirit/DS focussed character.<br /> <br /> How do you cope with these situations - specifically, when the player-driven plot requires everyone to sit out whilst a cabal-member goes on a short solo adventure? In our group, we have both of these types of characters - an ex-NWO refugee from The Feed who has signed on with the VA, and a Society of Ether &quot;ghostbuster&quot; with a focus in Dimensional Science. No one has a Sphere or Arete above 3 at the moment.<br /> <br /> What would you do if you wanted to include the rest of the cabal on a short jaunt through the Penumbra, or similar? On the one-hand, it's not really in keeping with the Sphere descriptions (Sp 4 for opening dimensional portals), but on the other hand I don't really want to park the other players whilst the DS person goes into the Upside-Down (haha). Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13778-cerulean-scream","name":"Cerulean Scream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T03:44:28-07:00","id":1128380,"title":"","content":"Give other players new characters to roleplay on player's quest together with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13055-goran","name":"Goran.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T05:12:25-07:00","id":1128392,"title":"","content":"The Spirit or Data expert is capable of sharing their senses with others, and even bringing them with them. If the PC is too weak to do so, then have an NPC handy who can help everyone get to the Plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T15:04:28-07:00","id":1128588,"title":"","content":"Good suggestions! I appreciate the ideas, guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13778-cerulean-scream","name":"Cerulean Scream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13778_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T00:53:43-07:00","id":1128727,"title":"","content":"I would also argue in favor of Spirit 3 being usable to bring others across the gauntlet.<br /> However, unlike with Spirit 4 and its ability to open up an actual portal though, you need to cast an effect and roll Arete for each individual to push/pull them across the Gauntlet, and you take Paradox each time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T09:54:38-07:00","id":1128860,"title":"","content":"Even if you don't rule that Spirit 3 can bring people along - it <i>would</i> undermine the utility of Spirit 4, after all - you have options. NPC mages can be brought in to open gates, or can give the cabal Wonders that do it for them (some kind of Talisman/Device, or a set of one-use Charms/Gadgets). There are also Shallowings - places where the Gauntlet is so thin, anyone can step through - that can allow the cabal access to the Umbra with little problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for jaunts through the Digital Web, it IS possible to access it without magick. VR tech is powerful enough now (especially in M20) that any mundane person - or person without the requisite Sphere levels - to access the Digital Web. They just need the right know-how to pull it off. And if you're bothering to go to the Digital Web, it's because there's at least one PC who knows how to do it; they can get everyone else set up and ready to dive. So unlike Cyberpunk and Shadowrun, this isn't as big a barrier in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}